. Sorry I can't give the experimental data  now because I'm running it on a very large data collections and currently I'm not allowed to public the data\n\n(1) When dealing with negative numbers, sometimes it gives [-117.-1,  1], This happens at the first bin index in my test case.\n(2) when bin# is two, it gives results like [1, 2005], (2005, 2005]\n(3)a bin result like this:  please note the value 0.993, and value 0.1\narray([[0.6, 0.991], (0.991, 0.992], (0.992, 0.993], (0.993, 0.993],\n       (0.993, 0.994], (0.994, 0.995], (0.995, 0.996], (0.996, 0.997],\n       (0.997, 0.998], (0.998, 0.1], (0.1, 1.2], (1.2, 1.5], (1.5, 2.1],\n       (2.1, 3.5], (3.5, 5.2], (5.2, 7.1], (7.1, 8.5], (8.5, 11],\n       (11, 13.7], (13.7, 65.8]], dtype=object)\n\n(2) and (3) might be caused by the same reason\n\nI'm using pandas 0.8.1 thanks.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/1979/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/1979/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":28455088,"node_id":"MDEzOkFzc2lnbmVkRXZlbnQyODQ1NTA4OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/events/28455088","actor":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"http